patch type="changed" "`ByteStreamReader.writeToFile` now creates its destination exclusively: if a file already exists at the path the write fails with `StreamError.io` and the existing file is left untouched, where it was previously replaced. A symlink at the destination is no longer followed to its target. The sender chooses the file name, so replacing whatever sits at that path was not a safe default — callers that relied on the overwrite must now pick an explicit destination or remove the file first"
